'brazil_task_configuration_schema@1.0'

// Flexible Build Tasks (FBT): split this package's fleet build into independent
// tasks that Brazil runs in parallel, then merges into one package output.
//
//   https://docs.hub.amazon.dev/languages/rust/cargobrazil-flexible-build-tasks/
//
// How it works:
//   - Each task's `arguments` names a `brazil-build` target, and that target
//     decides which phases run. The task `name` is just a free-form label.
//   - Every task starts with `configure` + `fetch` (each runs in its own
//     container), so FBT pays off only once a build has enough parallelizable
//     work to outweigh repeating those. On a small package the serial build is
//     already fast -- trim or delete tasks below if the split does not make your
//     build faster (verify with a dry-run build).
//   - Brazil reads this file FROM THE COMMIT before the build runs, so an
//     uncommitted or untracked file has no effect on the fleet. Locally,
//     `brazil-build` still runs the full serial build as usual.
//
// Edit freely: adjust `timeout_in_minutes`, rename tasks, or add/remove tasks.
// Keep task outputs disjoint (do not give two tasks the same target, and do not
// use `["release"]`) or the merge fails with a path conflict.
//
// To disable FBT entirely, delete this file and commit the deletion.

// Combine the parallel tasks' outputs into one result; fail on any path conflict.
task::merge_and_then_fail_on_path_conflict::{}

task:: {
    name: 'lint',
    timeout_in_minutes: 10,
    arguments: ["lint"],
}

task:: {
    name: 'test',
    timeout_in_minutes: 45,
    arguments: ["test"],
}

task:: {
    name: 'publish',
    timeout_in_minutes: 40,
    arguments: ["build"],
}
